      "source": "minerals/1-common/ores/gold-ore/index.md",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Gold Ore\nslug: gold-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Gold\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Gold Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"35% (+3 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 10 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Gold Ore\n\n## Effect\nGold Ore is rich in magical conductivity, making it one of the most valuable materials for enchantment despite its softness.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Tears of the Dawn,”* gold is believed to be crystallised sunlight buried within the earth.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Rare and valuable  \n- Soft and easily refined  \n- Highly magical  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Gold Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Sunsteel]] (future)\n- Reinforcement alloys\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Exceptional for divine and celestial magic  \n- Stabilises high-tier enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Gold does not fade — it remembers the light.\"*\n"
