      "content": "---\ntitle: \"Cavern Sprite\"\nslug: \"cavern-sprite\"\ntype: race\nraceCategory: \"Small Races\"\nsecondaryCategory: \"Sprite Races\"\ntertiaryCategory: \nplayable: true\nsize: \nmovement: \"8m (Walking)\"\nlanguages:\n  - \"Sprite - Common\"\nmagicAffinity:\n  - \"Dark Magic - Earth Magic\"\nessenceAffinity: []\ntags:\n  - \"race\"\n  - \"small-races\"\n  - \"sprite-races\"\nimages:\n  male: \"assets/races/cavern-sprite/cavern-sprite-male-adult.png\"\n  female: \"assets/races/cavern-sprite/cavern-sprite-female-adult.png\"\nvisibility: public\nsourceOrder: 27\n---\n\n# Cavern Sprite\n\n## Overview\n**Race Name:** Cavern Sprite  \n**Race Category:** Small Races\n**Race Type:** Sprite  \n**Size:** Small\n**Average Height:** 85–130 cm\n**Average Weight:** 18–55 kg  \n**Lifespan:** 180–260 years  \n**Home Region:** Deep Caverns, Crystal Hollows, Fungal Depths, Underground Ruins  \n**Primary Language:** Sprite Speak \n**Secondary Languages:** Common, Undercommon\n**Rarity:** Rare  \n**Alignment Tendencies:** Neutral Good, True Neutral, Chaotic Neutral\n\n# Cavern Sprite — Short Summary Paragraph\n\n> Cavern Sprites are small subterranean Feykin who dwell deep beneath the world within crystal caverns, fungal forests, and forgotten underground ruins. Known for their gray-toned skin, sharp elven features, and silent movements, they are masters of stealth, resonance, and survival within the endless dark. Curious yet cautious, Cavern Sprites preserve the balance of underground ecosystems and rarely trust surface dwellers.\n\n# Official Cavern Sprite Motto\n\n> **“Stone, Shadow, Silence.”**\n\n![[Pasted image 20260525214029.png]]\n\n## Racial Features\n- Height Range:\n  - 50 cm to 100 cm  \n\n- Weight Range:\n  - 10 kg to 25 kg  \n\n- Skin:\n  - Thin, smooth skin adapted to low light  \n  - Colour Range:\n    - Pale grey → charcoal → deep black  \n\n- Hair:\n  - Fine and soft, often uneven or naturally layered  \n  - Colour Range:\n    - Brown → ash → pale blonde  \n\n- Eyes:\n  - Large, slanted, highly sensitive to light  \n  - Colour Range:\n    - Grey → dark brown → near-black  \n  - Reflect light faintly in darkness  \n\n- Hands:\n  - Small, nimble fingers  \n  - Excellent grip for climbing and navigating tight spaces  \n\n- Face:\n  - Narrow features with sharp cheekbones  \n  - Expressions subtle and difficult to read  \n\n- Ears:\n  - Small with slight pointed tips  \n  - Highly sensitive to sound vibrations  \n\n- Markings:\n  - Faint dark patches or mineral-like streaks in skin  \n  - Some may have subtle glowing veins in deep darkness  \n\n- Body:\n  - Small, lightweight build  \n  - Movement is quick, quiet, and precise  \n\n---\n\n## Racial Characteristics\n| Characteristic | Buff/Debuff | Stat Rolls | Characteristic Tier Cap |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------- | :---------------------: |\n| Strength       | -4          | 3d6        |         Tier 2          |\n| Dexterity      | +1          | 4d6        |         Tier 5          |\n| Agility        | +2          | 4d6        |         Tier 5          |\n| Constitution   | -1          | 3d6        |         Tier 3          |\n| Endurance      | 0           | 3d6        |         Tier 4          |\n| Intelligence   | 0           | 4d6        |         Tier 4          |\n| Wisdom         | +1          | 4d6        |         Tier 5          |\n| Charisma       | 0           | 4d6        |         Tier 5          |\n| Luck           | 0           | 3d6        |         Tier 5          |\n\n---\n\n## Racial Traits\n### Racial Bond - Split Soul\n\n#### Description\nSprites are born with only half a soul. The missing half exists as a Pixie, creating an unbreakable spiritual bond that transcends distance and strengthens both when united.\n\n#### Effects\n- Every Sprite is spiritually bonded to a single Pixie.\n- Sprite and Pixie always know the general direction of one another.\n- The bond functions regardless of distance or plane unless magically severed.\n- When within close proximity, both gain improved magical harmony, reducing interference between magical abilities.\n- If the bond is damaged or severed, both creatures become **Unstable**, suffering narrative and mechanical consequences determined by the GM.\n\n---\n\n### Dark Vision\n\n#### Description\nGenerations beneath the earth have granted Cavern Sprites exceptional eyesight, allowing them to perceive clearly within darkness where most races would become completely blind.\n\n#### Effects\n- Can see clearly in darkness up to **30 metres**.\n- Suffers no vision penalties in low-light environments.\n- Distinguishes shapes, movement, and terrain in complete darkness.\n- Magical darkness still blocks vision unless otherwise stated.\n\n---\n\n### Light Footing\n\n#### Description\nCavern Sprites move effortlessly across uneven stone, instinctively placing each step with remarkable precision and allowing silent movement through caves and treacherous underground terrain.\n\n#### Effects\n- Ignore movement penalties caused by loose stone.\n- Ignore movement penalties caused by uneven cave terrain.\n- Reduce noise made while moving across rock and stone surfaces.\n- Gain Advantage on checks to maintain footing on natural cave terrain.\n\n---\n\n### Cavern Adaptation\n\n#### Description\nLife beneath the mountains has honed Cavern Sprites into expert navigators, enabling them to instinctively understand underground environments and recognise subtle changes within the surrounding stone.\n\n#### Effects\n- Gain Advantage on checks related to navigating caves.\n- Gain Advantage when detecting unstable cave structures.\n- Gain Advantage when locating hidden tunnels, passages, and natural caverns.\n- Can recognise common underground hazards with a successful appropriate skill check.\n\n---\n\n### Imbued Strike (Adapted)\n\n#### Description\nCavern Sprites naturally channel ambient subterranean mana through their bodies, allowing simple attacks and actions to carry traces of elemental power linked to their homeland.\n\n#### Effects\n- May imbue attacks or actions with **Earth** or **Dark** elemental energy.\n- Grants a minor magical effect appropriate to the chosen element.\n- Does not increase base damage unless specified by another ability.\n- Scales through future racial abilities, talents, and progression systems.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Culture\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Historical Figures\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Settlements\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Relations\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Traits & Biology\n- Small size allows movement through tight spaces  \n- Can climb rocky surfaces with reduced difficulty  \n- Gains stealth advantage in darkness  \n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Drawbacks\n- Very low physical strength  \n- Fragile compared to larger races  \n- Sensitive to bright light (possible disadvantage in strong light)\n\n## Gallery\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## GM Notes\nGM-only information coming soon.\n"
